quran[11]{c,v,t}:
  29,53,"And they ask you to hasten the punishment. Had the time not been specified, the punishment would have surely come to them. And indeed, it will overtake them suddenly while they are unaware."
  29,54,"They challenge you to hasten the punishment. Indeed, Hell will besiege the disbelievers."
  29,55,"On the Day the punishment will overwhelm them from above them and from beneath their feet, He will say: ‘Taste what you used to do!’"
  29,56,"O My servants who believe! Indeed, My earth is vast. Therefore, Me alone should you worship."
  29,57,Every soul shall taste death. Then you shall be brought back to Us.
  29,58,"And those who believe and perform righteous deeds, We will surely settle them in lofty dwellings of Paradise, (graced) with streams flowing beneath them, remaining therein forever. How excellent is the reward of the righteous workers,"
  29,59,those who are patient and put their trust in their Lord!
  29,60,"How many creatures do not carry their provision, but Allah provides for them and you (as well)? And He is the All-Hearing, the All-Knowing."
  29,61,"If you ask them: ‘Who created the heavens and the earth and subjected the sun and the moon?’ they will surely say: ‘Allah.’ How, then, do they turn away?"
  29,62,"Allah expands (the means of) provision for whom He pleases among His servants and straitens it for whom (He wills). Indeed, Allah is All-Knowing of everything."
  29,63,"If you ask them: ‘Who sends down water from the sky, then gives life to the earth with it after its death?’ they will surely say: ‘Allah.’ Say: ‘All praise belongs to Allah!’ But most of them have no understanding."
